infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two write shapes: blind append vs idempotent write
  desc Re-running a stage must replace state, not add rows
  compares
    - label Blind append
      children
        - label Retry doubles the day's rows
          desc Scheduler retry or human rerun re-emits everything
        - label Nothing to roll back
          desc Object stores and file sinks have no transaction
        - label Recovery is forensic dedupe
          desc Must reconstruct what the failed attempt wrote
        - label Backfill is an emergency script
          desc Hand-edited, with now() baked in
    - label Idempotent write
      children
        - label Overwrite the window partition
          desc Write dt=YYYY-MM-DD/ and replace it wholesale
        - label Or merge on a business key
          desc Upsert into a table sink instead of appending
        - label Retry replaces state, not adds
          desc Same input window yields the same state
        - label Backfill is a parameter
          desc Watermark processes only newer partitions
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
